{"agreement":1.0,"case":901,"commit":"9ca7313b945f2a8360251394bac2e05352eaf729","event":"vote","hash":"ca8a5b822cda21bd9d01052d91df7a68fcac1c71487bbf3241283a43611532c8","invocation":"20261009T154407.463516+0000-50887","outcome":"carried","prev":"e8a3a4b2dab96dc8588f028c4cb6c668af3b259473593a5670fe93c330290ad7","prompts":"5b8510cd900aa9da58e06fd2a865f94df5ede1bdb3c73006077576411858ea61","proposals":[{"amount_sgd":4.0,"driver_compensation_sgd":4.0,"referrals":[],"ruling":"DRIVER_COMPENSATION"},{"amount_sgd":4.0,"driver_compensation_sgd":4.0,"referrals":[],"ruling":"DRIVER_COMPENSATION"},{"amount_sgd":4.0,"driver_compensation_sgd":4.0,"referrals":[],"ruling":"DRIVER_COMPENSATION"},{"amount_sgd":4.0,"driver_compensation_sgd":4.0,"referrals":[],"ruling":"DRIVER_COMPENSATION"}],"seq":35,"threshold":3,"ts":"2026-10-09T15:46:58.799566+00:00","unanimous":true,"valid":4,"votes":4}
{"case":901,"commit":"9ca7313b945f2a8360251394bac2e05352eaf729","event":"ruling","failed_agent":null,"failure_reason":null,"findings":0,"hash":"961f4afa0f67898c40d5575b944c0a88f6948345959f4a9ea213015a452cb16b","invocation":"20261009T154407.463516+0000-50887","prev":"ca8a5b822cda21bd9d01052d91df7a68fcac1c71487bbf3241283a43611532c8","prompts":"5b8510cd900aa9da58e06fd2a865f94df5ede1bdb3c73006077576411858ea61","ruling":{"amount_sgd":4.0,"confidence":0.9,"driver_compensation_sgd":4.0,"explanation":"To the rider (R-7823): your $5.00 no-show cancellation fee is upheld and stands charged, and $4.00 of it is paid to the driver. To the driver (D-2398): your fee stands and your payout is confirmed at $4.00.\n\nWhat decides the case. Trip TRIP-2026-09945 was booked 08:30, the driver assigned 08:30:15, and the platform recorded its own arrival measurement at 08:43:00 — 'Driver GPS within 10m of pickup point. Speed 0 km/h. Auto-arrival confirmed.' — because trip_record.platform_policy.arrival_marker is GPS_AUTO. The platform then notified the rider at 08:43:05, started the free 5-minute wait timer at 08:43:10, called the rider in-app at 08:47:05 (22 s, unanswered), marked the free wait expired at 08:48:10, and terminated the trip at 08:51:00 under cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW, charging the $5.00 fee (EV-TRIP-00901). POL-NS-12 applies: with a GPS_AUTO marker, the platform's own arrival event (distance and speed) plus wait_timer_started and wait_timer_expired are its full-resolution measurement and an independent carrier for POL-NS-01 limbs (b) and (c) — arrival is established at 08:43:00, and the free waiting period is established as served at 08:48:10. No admissible fix places the driver outside the arrival radius or moving at 15 km/h, so the POL-NS-12 exception and POL-NS-05 do not fire. POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full: (a) an 'arrived' event exists; (b) arrival is established from the platform's own measurement; (c) the dwell from 08:43:10 to 08:48:10 is the 300 s platform_policy.free_wait_sec requires, and the 08:51:00 cancellation is 480 s after arrival, meeting platform_policy.no_show_threshold_sec of 480 s; (d) no boarding was recorded and the driver terminated with RIDER_NO_SHOW, one of the three reason codes limb (d) recognises. No clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces the fee, so POL-NS-07 fixes the driver's payout.\n\nThe rider's arguments, answered. The rider's case rests on the exported trace EV-GPS-00901, which is impaired (weight 0.6, issues LOW_SAMPLE_RATE and PARTIAL_RECORD) and reports no horizontal accuracy on any of its eight fixes. The rider argues that under POL-NS-02 no qualifying in-radius fix exists, so the driver never arrived and limb (b) fails, and that under POL-NS-06 the effective in-geofence dwell is 0 s against the required 300 s, so the fee must be fully refunded. Both are rejected. POL-NS-12 is directed at exactly this situation: a sparse or accuracy-less export does not impair the platform's own arrival and wait-timer events, which establish arrival and the waiting period served. The derived qualifying_fix_count of 0 and accumulated_dwell of 0 s are the 25 m accuracy filter operating on an export that reports no accuracy at all, not measurements that the driver was elsewhere; under POL-NS-02 an accuracy-less fix is evidence of neither presence nor absence. There is no waiting-period shortfall for POL-NS-06 to refund. The rider's point that POL-NS-12 does not reach POL-NS-06 is not accepted: POL-NS-12 establishes the free waiting period as served for POL-NS-01 limb (c), and POL-NS-06's shortfall test is measured against that period, so it finds nothing to refund. The rider is correct that the MISSING traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00901-01 (weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT) makes POL-NS-06 limb (i) unavailable, but it decides nothing because there is no shortfall to accumulate across. The rider is also correct that no rider track was supplied, so POL-NS-04 limb (c) is UNDECIDABLE and neutral under POL-NS-11 rather than adverse — and that too decides nothing, because the fee rests on the driver's evidence. The rider is right that the chat log EV-CHAT-00901 holds no rider message (all six entries are the driver's or the system's) so POL-NS-04 limb (a) fails and cannot exonerate the rider; the driver's in-app call and messages defeat limb (b) in any event.\n\nThe driver's case, answered. I accept that the fee stands and that POL-NS-07 fixes the payout: 80 percent of the $5.00 fee in force (read from trip_record.platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd as fee_schedule.resolution_rule directs) is $4.00, which the fare ledger's derived money block also computes (EV-FARE-00901, impaired, weight 0.75, issue PARTIAL_RECORD). The anti-farming check does not withhold it: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is null, so the '4 or more' limb is not met and the check is undecidable rather than tripped. The driver is right that POL-NS-05 is not engaged (the marker was auto-confirmed at 10 m and 0 km/h and no admissible fix contradicts it), that POL-NS-03 is not reached, and that the ledger's $5.00 line equals the fee in force, so POL-NS-08(d) is not engaged.\n\nOutcome and amounts. The rider's claim is not supported on the fee, which stays charged (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00, EV-FARE-00901). Because the verified no-show also produces a driver payment, the ruling is DRIVER_COMPENSATION, and under POL-GEN-03 amount_sgd mirrors driver_compensation_sgd at $4.00 — that is the amount the ruling moves, not a refund to the filing party. The monetary effect ($4.00) is within the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of $8.00, so it executes automatically on issue, subject to the appeal route under POL-GEN-04.\n\nConfidence. The deciding facts — arrival, the waiting period served, and termination for a rider no-show — are carried by EV-TRIP-00901 (weight 1.0) and EV-CHAT-00901 (weight 1.0), which POL-NS-12 makes independent of the export; the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is therefore 1.0 and confidence is 0.9, above the 0.70 floor. The impaired fare ledger (0.75) and export (0.6) do not carry the deciding facts.\n\nDiscarded claims. The referee discarded four claims for citing an impaired artifact without disclosing its issue codes; they are recorded in discarded_claims and form no part of this ruling. Nothing here turns on the rider's prior_no_show_flags of 1, which POL-GEN-01 makes context only and which is not the trailing-window field POL-NS-09(d) names.\n\nThe judge was asked 4 times on the same inputs and every draft agreed on this ruling, so it is carried unanimously (vote agreement 1.00).","referrals":[],"ruling":"DRIVER_COMPENSATION"},"seq":36,"ts":"2026-10-09T15:46:58.800182+00:00"}
